#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0719 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a BDS dataset contains none of the subject-level or record-level treatment variables defined in the IG.
#note "Only TRT1A is present: a one-digit index is no member of the TRTxxA family (xx is exactly two digits, the IG's 01-99), so count(find_vars('TRTxxA')) == 0 holds and, with none of the other 25 treatment variables present, the rule fires once for the dataset (PLAN-dynamic-column-corpus-respelling phase 2 — pins the template's width, as CDISC-AD0581's invalid_trt1p_only does)."
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL type=Num
col TRT1A type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 12.5 | X
---
